@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 100
title Lecture change and push notification
autonumber
participant "Professor" as U
participant "Lecture editor / Cubit" as UI
participant "Lecture change / read use cases" as D
participant "TimetableRepositoryImpl / Firestore data source" as R
participant "Cloud Firestore + rules" as F
participant "Lecture-change Cloud Function" as C
participant "Firebase Cloud Messaging" as M
participant "Student device / app" as S
note over U, S: Preconditions: professor teaches the course; affected students have registered device tokens and enabled notifications.
U -> UI: Change room / times, or cancel with optional reason
UI -> D: Submit change; show loading
D -> D: Validate required room and end after start for reschedule
alt Invalid input
D --> UI: Failure; show validation message
else Valid input
D -> R: rescheduleLecture(...) or cancelLecture(...)
R -> F: Update lectures/{id}; enforce assigned-professor access
alt Permission denied or write fails
F --> R: Write error
R --> D: Failure(AppFailure)
D --> UI: Failure; show error, no notification triggered
else Write committed
F --> R: Committed lecture update
R --> D: Success(Lecture) or Success(void)
D --> UI: Show saved change (not a delivery receipt)
group Asynchronous notification after commit
F -> C: Lecture update event: before / after / event ID
C -> C: Ignore unchanged room, times and status; deduplicate retries
C -> F: Query course enrolments and users.fcmTokens
F --> C: Affected students and registration tokens
C -> M: Send batched alert with lectureId and event ID
M --> C: Per-token acceptance or send error
C -> C: Remove invalid tokens; retry transient failures
M -> S: Deliver notification when possible
S -> S: Tap: session guard opens lecture details
S -> D: Read current lecture through domain use case
D -> R: Fetch authorized lecture details
R -> F: Read lectures/{id} under security rules
F --> R: Current lecture or access / network error
R --> D: Result
D --> S: Display current state or error
end
end
end
note over U, S: Push is best effort; delivery failure never rolls back the lecture. Firestore remains the source of truth.
@enduml
